1
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:07,200
What a coincidence.

2
00:00:08,519 --> 00:00:09,919
I got Dad

3
00:00:09,919 --> 00:00:11,320
a painting too.

4
00:00:12,439 --> 00:00:13,240
Show us.

5
00:00:21,719 --> 00:00:22,719
Impossible.

6
00:00:23,120 --> 00:00:25,440
I reserved this painting six months ago.

7
00:00:27,519 --> 00:00:28,559
Huan...

8
00:00:28,559 --> 00:00:31,719
Yours isn't a fake, is it?

9
00:00:33,840 --> 00:00:34,920
I was about to

10
00:00:34,920 --> 00:00:36,240
ask you the same.

11
00:00:42,039 --> 00:00:42,840
Song Cheng.

12
00:00:44,320 --> 00:00:46,200
Why don't you take a look

13
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:47,560
at these two paintings?

14
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:48,560
Which one's real,

15
00:00:48,560 --> 00:00:49,359
and which one's fake?

16
00:00:56,560 --> 00:00:58,439
Mr. Song. Ladies.

17
00:00:58,560 --> 00:01:00,920
I majored in art appreciation.

18
00:01:01,159 --> 00:01:03,320
To make a fake look real,

19
00:01:03,320 --> 00:01:05,319
forgers copy the original closely,

20
00:01:05,719 --> 00:01:07,840
but often overlook little details,

21
00:01:07,840 --> 00:01:08,959
like the frames.

22
00:01:09,200 --> 00:01:11,040
From what I know, this artist

23
00:01:11,040 --> 00:01:13,159
preferred wooden frames.

24
00:01:13,560 --> 00:01:14,519
Ms. Song Cheng.

25
00:01:14,519 --> 00:01:16,040
You love woodworking.

26
00:01:16,159 --> 00:01:19,040
Could you spot clues in their frames?

27
00:01:27,719 --> 00:01:28,560
(That way,)

28
00:01:28,760 --> 00:01:30,359
(I made what Song Cheng does best)

29
00:01:30,560 --> 00:01:32,359
=Dear Song=
(the key to solving this.)

30
00:01:32,380 --> 00:01:35,160
=Episode 3=
(The Flaw)

31
00:01:35,560 --> 00:01:36,599
Could you please

32
00:01:36,599 --> 00:01:38,680
bring the paintings closer?

33
00:01:47,640 --> 00:01:48,439
Yu Song.

34
00:01:49,319 --> 00:01:51,200
Could you check

35
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:52,760
the corners of both frames?

36
00:02:16,120 --> 00:02:18,759
I paid two million for it at auction.

37
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:20,319
Be careful.

38
00:02:30,560 --> 00:02:31,639
Ms. Song Cheng.

39
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:34,520
Both frames are finely crafted.

40
00:02:34,919 --> 00:02:36,639
But Ms. Song Lin's frame

41
00:02:36,800 --> 00:02:37,840
has especially sharp edges.

42
00:02:38,120 --> 00:02:39,719
It nearly cut through my glove.

43
00:02:40,599 --> 00:02:41,360
Lin.

44
00:02:41,879 --> 00:02:43,400
Your painting is a fake.

45
00:02:43,599 --> 00:02:44,520
That's nonsense!

46
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:45,960
Just from the frame,

47
00:02:45,960 --> 00:02:47,319
you call mine a fake?

48
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:49,000
Frames for famous art

49
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:50,719
are usually handmade.

50
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:52,719
When carving the wood,

51
00:02:52,719 --> 00:02:53,960
to avoid injury,

52
00:02:54,319 --> 00:02:55,919
carpenters use chisels

53
00:02:55,919 --> 00:02:57,319
to bevel the edges

54
00:02:57,520 --> 00:02:59,319
and round off the corners.

55
00:03:00,560 --> 00:03:02,360
But machine-cut edges,

56
00:03:02,360 --> 00:03:03,840
like these, stay sharp.

57
00:03:04,560 --> 00:03:05,360
Yu Song.

58
00:03:05,919 --> 00:03:07,479
Could you smell

59
00:03:07,479 --> 00:03:08,960
where the frame joins?

60
00:03:09,199 --> 00:03:10,680
See if there's

61
00:03:10,680 --> 00:03:12,319
a faint sour smell.

62
00:03:25,599 --> 00:03:26,800
It does smell sour.

63
00:03:29,800 --> 00:03:30,599
Then that's it.

64
00:03:31,120 --> 00:03:33,639
To preserve the wood's scent,

65
00:03:34,719 --> 00:03:37,759
carpenters use natural adhesives.

66
00:03:38,319 --> 00:03:39,960
Quick-drying glue,

67
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:41,960
on the other hand, smells faintly sour.

68
00:03:42,520 --> 00:03:43,479
However,

69
00:03:43,479 --> 00:03:46,439
these are just basic frame observations.

70
00:03:46,599 --> 00:03:48,000
For the next step,

71
00:03:48,439 --> 00:03:51,120
we should contact
an art authentication firm.

72
00:03:51,599 --> 00:03:52,520
I'm fine with that.

73
00:03:54,719 --> 00:03:55,520
Fine.

74
00:03:55,520 --> 00:03:56,919
Let's have them authenticated.

75
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:01,520
Jing.

76
00:04:02,360 --> 00:04:05,120
Take both paintings to my study.

77
00:04:09,840 --> 00:04:10,919
Come here.

78
00:04:14,120 --> 00:04:15,479
My daughters' thoughtfulness

79
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:17,319
is what matters most.

80
00:04:21,600 --> 00:04:22,800
Mr. Song said

81
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:25,279
it's the thought that counts.

82
00:04:33,839 --> 00:04:34,639
Dad.

83
00:04:35,279 --> 00:04:36,399
A few days ago,

84
00:04:36,680 --> 00:04:39,079
I noticed your float case was worn out.

85
00:04:39,600 --> 00:04:41,000
So I made you a new one.

86
00:04:41,399 --> 00:04:43,319
I used your favorite walnut wood.

87
00:04:44,399 --> 00:04:45,439
Happy birthday.

88
00:04:46,480 --> 00:04:47,000
Okay.

89
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:47,800
Let me see.

90
00:05:01,439 --> 00:05:02,240
Cheng.

91
00:05:03,319 --> 00:05:04,399
I love it.

92
00:05:05,720 --> 00:05:07,399
I'm going fishing
the day after tomorrow.

93
00:05:07,920 --> 00:05:08,800
Come with me.

94
00:05:11,480 --> 00:05:12,000
Dad.

95
00:05:12,120 --> 00:05:14,839
Song Huan and I used to fish with you.

96
00:05:16,120 --> 00:05:17,079
I have a business trip abroad.

97
00:05:17,079 --> 00:05:18,000
I don't have time.

98
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:19,639
But I'm free!

99
00:05:19,639 --> 00:05:20,399
What?

100
00:05:20,759 --> 00:05:22,560
Do I need your permission

101
00:05:22,560 --> 00:05:23,639
to decide who I go fishing with?

102
00:05:24,639 --> 00:05:25,439
No...

103
00:05:27,279 --> 00:05:28,160
Congrats.

104
00:05:28,639 --> 00:05:30,000
One step closer to your goal.

105
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:32,439
When I was little,

106
00:05:32,720 --> 00:05:34,519
they called me "Stinky Fish Beggar"

107
00:05:34,920 --> 00:05:36,360
because my dad sold fish.

108
00:05:36,959 --> 00:05:38,959
No matter how much I washed my hands,

109
00:05:39,439 --> 00:05:41,920
they'd hold their noses and run away,

110
00:05:42,560 --> 00:05:44,959
as if I'd leave them smelling like fish.

111
00:05:46,319 --> 00:05:47,560
I love wearing perfume.

112
00:05:48,639 --> 00:05:49,680
The stronger, the better.

113
00:05:52,800 --> 00:05:54,000
The stronger the scent,

114
00:05:55,079 --> 00:05:56,439
the safer I feel.

115
00:06:01,800 --> 00:06:03,399
Even after Dad died,

116
00:06:04,279 --> 00:06:06,199
the fish smell was long gone.

117
00:06:09,319 --> 00:06:11,800
Later
I had to live under my uncle's roof.

118
00:06:12,240 --> 00:06:13,920
I was expelled in my junior year.

119
00:06:15,600 --> 00:06:18,600
They threatened to sell me off
to a crippled old man to bear him a son.

120
00:06:19,399 --> 00:06:21,000
So I ran as hard as I could,

121
00:06:21,480 --> 00:06:22,920
trying to escape it all.

122
00:06:24,399 --> 00:06:25,920
I just wanted a better life.

123
00:06:26,839 --> 00:06:27,639
Tell me,

124
00:06:30,319 --> 00:06:31,600
what did I do wrong?

125
00:06:33,720 --> 00:06:35,480
But why choose the Song family?

126
00:06:35,480 --> 00:06:37,000
If I'm risking my life,

127
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:38,959
I'll choose the biggest prize.

128
00:06:39,879 --> 00:06:41,439
I'll put Song Cheng

129
00:06:41,439 --> 00:06:43,519
at the heart of the family's power.

130
00:06:43,800 --> 00:06:44,920
That's my plan.

131
00:06:45,399 --> 00:06:46,319
Dating me...

132
00:06:47,319 --> 00:06:48,920
Is that part of your plan?

133
00:06:54,079 --> 00:06:55,279
We're two of a kind.

134
00:06:58,759 --> 00:07:00,480
We're meant to be.

135
00:07:36,720 --> 00:07:38,680
We usually use a whole worm as bait.

136
00:07:39,319 --> 00:07:40,600
What's your trick?

137
00:07:42,399 --> 00:07:46,000
Dad, why use only half a worm for bait?

138
00:07:46,120 --> 00:07:46,920
Lately...

139
00:07:46,920 --> 00:07:48,319
Fish haven't sold well.

140
00:07:48,519 --> 00:07:50,800
So we save where we can.

141
00:07:51,199 --> 00:07:51,879
Song.

142
00:07:52,079 --> 00:07:54,399
Don't underestimate half a worm.

143
00:07:54,519 --> 00:07:57,720
The fluids it releases

144
00:07:57,800 --> 00:07:59,720
make fish bite more easily.

145
00:07:59,720 --> 00:08:00,279
Got it?

146
00:08:00,279 --> 00:08:02,120
You're amazing, Dad!

147
00:08:02,439 --> 00:08:05,120
I learned this old trick from fishermen
while I was at sea overseas.

148
00:08:05,319 --> 00:08:06,800
When they were low on cash,

149
00:08:06,800 --> 00:08:08,600
they'd use this to save on bait.

150
00:08:08,920 --> 00:08:11,600
And the fluid a cut worm gives off

151
00:08:11,600 --> 00:08:13,680
is a deadly lure for big fish.

152
00:08:14,319 --> 00:08:15,199
Give it a try.

153
00:08:16,199 --> 00:08:17,000
Okay.

154
00:08:26,920 --> 00:08:27,800
Here we go.

155
00:08:36,720 --> 00:08:37,399
Yu Song.

156
00:08:37,639 --> 00:08:39,000
With you here for Cheng,

157
00:08:39,480 --> 00:08:40,279
I'm at ease.

158
00:08:40,720 --> 00:08:42,080
What Ms. Song Cheng needs most

159
00:08:42,080 --> 00:08:43,600
is her father's company.

160
00:08:43,919 --> 00:08:46,440
She heard she'd be fishing with you,

161
00:08:46,440 --> 00:08:48,000
and was too excited to sleep.

162
00:09:10,799 --> 00:09:11,600
Cheng.

163
00:09:11,600 --> 00:09:14,320
I haven't been there for you enough.

164
00:09:15,799 --> 00:09:16,600
No.

165
00:09:17,200 --> 00:09:19,000
Just fishing with you like this

166
00:09:19,600 --> 00:09:21,000
makes me so happy.

167
00:09:22,600 --> 00:09:23,399
All right.

168
00:09:23,519 --> 00:09:24,320
Let's get back to fishing.

169
00:09:24,799 --> 00:09:25,600
Mm.

170
00:09:43,080 --> 00:09:46,900
(Song's Disabled Youngest Daughter
Rarely Seen; Song Huaishan Shows Warmth)

171
00:09:49,759 --> 00:09:52,039
The public had forgotten
that brat even existed!

172
00:09:52,039 --> 00:09:53,759
Now they all remember!

173
00:09:54,480 --> 00:09:55,279
Honey.

174
00:09:56,159 --> 00:09:58,120
You've been Dad's favorite
since you were little.

175
00:09:58,639 --> 00:10:01,240
Song Cheng's disabled, anyway.

176
00:10:01,519 --> 00:10:03,440
She's no threat to us.

177
00:10:04,080 --> 00:10:06,440
It's Song Huan we need to worry about.

178
00:10:23,279 --> 00:10:24,639
So...

179
00:10:24,919 --> 00:10:26,399
That hot spring project,

180
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:28,840
you must win it.

181
00:10:30,440 --> 00:10:33,039
If Song Huan takes it again,

182
00:10:33,960 --> 00:10:35,360
you know the consequences.

183
00:10:47,279 --> 00:10:47,759
Yu Song.

184
00:10:48,360 --> 00:10:49,320
Thank you.

185
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:51,639
It's been so long

186
00:10:52,039 --> 00:10:54,120
since I spent time with Dad like this.

187
00:10:54,279 --> 00:10:55,360
Why thank me?

188
00:10:55,960 --> 00:10:57,360
What Mr. Song saw

189
00:10:57,360 --> 00:10:58,559
was how much you care about him.

190
00:11:01,720 --> 00:11:02,759
It's getting late.

191
00:11:03,159 --> 00:11:04,799
Time for bed.

192
00:11:04,799 --> 00:11:05,600
Mm.

193
00:11:07,360 --> 00:11:08,960
Here, hold on to me.

194
00:11:16,679 --> 00:11:17,519
Ms. Song Cheng...

195
00:11:19,120 --> 00:11:20,840
Sorry I didn't hold you steady.

196
00:11:22,759 --> 00:11:23,559
It's okay.

197
00:11:23,879 --> 00:11:25,279
I won't let you fall again.

198
00:11:32,120 --> 00:11:33,080
Ms. Song Huan.

199
00:11:34,879 --> 00:11:35,559
Ms. Chen.

200
00:11:35,559 --> 00:11:37,480
Ms. Song Cheng has gone to bed.

201
00:11:37,480 --> 00:11:38,679
May I leave now?

202
00:11:40,120 --> 00:11:41,879
Dad's blood sugar's been high.

203
00:11:42,799 --> 00:11:44,639
These plums came from France.

204
00:11:44,840 --> 00:11:45,720
You can have them.

205
00:11:48,840 --> 00:11:50,720
Really, Ms. Song Huan?

206
00:11:52,080 --> 00:11:52,919
Thank you.

207
00:11:55,240 --> 00:11:56,320
I meant her.

208
00:11:59,600 --> 00:12:00,799
She means you.

209
00:12:01,399 --> 00:12:02,879
What are you waiting for?

210
00:12:02,879 --> 00:12:04,000
She's giving those to you.

211
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:05,039
Just take it!

212
00:12:05,679 --> 00:12:07,120
Quit the act.

213
00:12:16,679 --> 00:12:18,000
Thank you, Ms. Song Huan.

214
00:12:24,039 --> 00:12:25,440
I'll be going, then.

215
00:12:51,519 --> 00:12:52,600
This house...

216
00:12:53,360 --> 00:12:55,200
finally has someone interesting in it.

217
00:13:13,679 --> 00:13:15,200
So fruit picked in the morning

218
00:13:15,200 --> 00:13:18,120
and eaten that night tastes like this.

219
00:13:18,399 --> 00:13:20,399
It's not just the fruity flavor.

220
00:13:20,440 --> 00:13:23,039
It tastes fresh and full of life.

221
00:13:24,080 --> 00:13:25,240
Why are you eating it like that?

222
00:13:26,879 --> 00:13:28,679
I just wanted to see

223
00:13:29,240 --> 00:13:30,320
what it would taste like

224
00:13:30,799 --> 00:13:32,320
if I mixed

225
00:13:35,039 --> 00:13:36,200
what I have

226
00:13:36,200 --> 00:13:37,320
with what I want.

227
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:39,200
So, how does it taste?

228
00:13:48,240 --> 00:13:49,399
Like success.

229
00:13:53,480 --> 00:13:55,200
This photographer's good.

230
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:58,320
When Song Huaishan's alone
with Song Cheng,

231
00:13:58,320 --> 00:13:59,480
have her photograph them again.

232
00:13:59,799 --> 00:14:02,320
I'll get Song Cheng trending online
as the Song family's princess.

233
00:14:02,840 --> 00:14:05,320
When people mention the Song family,

234
00:14:05,879 --> 00:14:07,679
they won't just think of
Song Huan and Song Lin.

235
00:14:10,639 --> 00:14:11,720
But I like this one more.

236
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:16,039
Soon...

237
00:14:16,039 --> 00:14:19,200
I'll become the person she trusts most.

238
00:14:19,600 --> 00:14:22,840
(Song Group, Real Estate)
Once I map their ties,

239
00:14:23,240 --> 00:14:24,240
the next step

240
00:14:24,240 --> 00:14:26,519
is to find the right moment

241
00:14:26,519 --> 00:14:28,480
to get Song Cheng into Song Group.

242
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:30,159
Through her,

243
00:14:30,159 --> 00:14:32,399
I'll control Song Group's core business.

244
00:14:38,200 --> 00:14:39,240
I want a shower.

245
00:14:39,399 --> 00:14:40,320
Want to join me?

246
00:14:40,639 --> 00:14:41,440
Let's go.

247
00:14:47,840 --> 00:14:50,279
(Enjoying this game of lies?)

248
00:14:50,519 --> 00:14:51,879
Who's this?

249
00:14:54,600 --> 00:14:55,799
Whoever it is,

250
00:14:56,840 --> 00:14:58,600
they won't interfere with my plan.

251
00:15:00,639 --> 00:15:01,679
Aren't you going to reply to him

252
00:15:02,200 --> 00:15:03,000
and ask him to meet up?

253
00:15:03,399 --> 00:15:05,120
He contacted me first,

254
00:15:05,120 --> 00:15:06,399
instead of handing the info

255
00:15:06,399 --> 00:15:08,480
straight to Song Huaishan.

256
00:15:08,799 --> 00:15:10,639
He must want something from me.

257
00:15:17,639 --> 00:15:19,000
He'll come to me on his own.
